Package: leafblower
Title: High-Performance Bounded Survey Weight Calibration
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Dennis Alexis Valin", "Dittrich",
    email = "davdittrich@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Dennis Alexis Valin Dittrich [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Dennis Alexis Valin Dittrich <davdittrich@gmail.com>
Description: Drop-in replacement for autumn::harvest() providing multiple
    bounded survey-weight calibration solvers: ORIS (box-constrained Sinkhorn
    block-coordinate descent), raking, Sinkhorn, Greenkhorn, GREG and logit
    (Deville-Sarndal linear and logit duals), Chebyshev interior-point, and
    Newton-KL. Adds min_weight and max_weight bounds; shares a single C++17
    core with the Python bindings.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: yes
SystemRequirements: C++17 compiler, OpenMP (optional, for SIMD exp vectorisation)
Imports: stats
Suggests: autumn (>= 0.2.0), testthat (>= 3.0.0), bench, lhs, DiceKriging, ggplot2, rprojroot,
    survey, PracTools (>= 1.4.0)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Config/testthat/edition: 3
